The '''2021–22 South African Premiership''' (known as the '''[[South African Premier Division|DSTV Premiership]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 26th season of the Premier Soccer League since its establishment in [[1996–97 Premier Soccer League|1996]].  It was played from 20 August 2021 to 30 May 2022. [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]] won the title for the fifth consecutive year, qualifying for the [[2022–23 CAF Champions League]] along with [[Cape Town City F.C. (2016)|Cape Town City]]. [[Royal AM F.C.|Royal AM]] and [[2021–22 Nedbank Cup|Nedbank Cup]] runners-up [[Marumo Gallants F.C.|Marumo Gallants]] qualified for the [[2022–23 CAF Confederation Cup]].

==Team changes==

The following teams changed division since the 2020–21 season.

