* [[Black Leopards F.C.|Black Leopards]]

===From National First Division===
'''Promoted to 2021–22 South African Premiership'''
* [[Sekhukhune United F.C.|Sekhukhune United]] (promoted as champions)<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-06-12 |title=Official: Sekhukhune United promoted to DStv Premiership |url=https://www.kickoff.com/news/articles/south-africa-news/categories/news/premiership/official-sekhukhune-united-promoted-to-dstv-premiership/700681 |access-date=2021-08-27 |website=Kick Off}}</ref>

===Purchased statuses===
* [[Marumo Gallants F.C.|Marumo Gallants]] purchased their status from [[Tshakhuma Tsha Madzivhandila F.C.|Tshakhuma Tsha Madzivhandila]]<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-08-17 |title=New name, new owners but same old problems! Inside the mess of Marumo Gallants ahead of the new season |url=https://www.thesouthafrican.com/sport/soccer/psl-south-africa/new-name-new-owners-but-same-old-problems-inside-the-mess-of-marumo-gallants-ahead-of-the-new-season/ |access-date=2021-08-27 |website=The South African |language=en-ZA |archive-date=28 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220528053203/https://www.thesouthafrican.com/sport/soccer/psl-south-africa/new-name-new-owners-but-same-old-problems-inside-the-mess-of-marumo-gallants-ahead-of-the-new-season/ |url-status=dead}}</ref>
* [[Royal AM F.C.|Royal AM]] purchased their Premiership status from [[Bloemfontein Celtic F.C.|Bloemfontein Celtic]]<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-08-17 |title=Bloemfontein Celtic sold: Renamed Royal AM |url=https://en.africatopsports.com/2021/08/17/dstv-premiership-bloemfontein-celtic-sold-renamed-royal-am/ |access-date=2021-08-27 |website=Africa Top Sports |language=en-US |archive-date=17 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250317203057/https://en.africatopsports.com/2021/08/17/dstv-premiership-bloemfontein-celtic-sold-renamed-royal-am/ |url-status=dead}}</ref>

